Specification UserInterface

Description The windows the program is worked in: a list of accounts, the
Description register of the account selected in it, and an optional second pane
Description that shows either another account or an import waiting to be reviewed.
Details
Details The shape is three regions. On the left, every account, grouped by the
Details kind of thing it is. On the right, the register of whichever account is
Details selected. The right may be split in two, so that two accounts can be
Details read at once -- or so that an import can be looked over beside the
Details register it is about to change.
Details
Details What is specified here is what the windows show and what selecting
Details things does. Pixels, fonts and column widths are not: those are not
Details worth agreeing in a table, and changing them should not fail a test.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The account list
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DataType AccountGroup
Description The headings the account list is divided into. One per kind of real
Description account, and the categories are not in the list at all: they are
Description reached through a report, not browsed.
Details The words Asset and Liability are not headings here. Which side of a
Details balance sheet an account is on is a different question, asked by the
Details balance sheet and nowhere else; see the balance-side rule in CoreTypes.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value            | Notes                                      |
| Banking          | Checking, savings and cash                 |
| Credit           | What is owed on a card or a line of credit |
| Investments      | Holdings and their cash                    |
| LoanAndDebt      | A mortgage or a loan                       |
| PropertyAndAsset | A house, a car, anything else owned        |
| Business         | What is owed to and by the business        |
| Transfer         | Money on its way between two accounts      |

BusinessRule Which group an account is listed under and how the heading reads
Description Taken from the account type, so nothing has to be filed by hand.
Details The nominal types have no group: Income, Expense and Equity are
Details categories and the account list does not show them. Their heading is
Details given here as an empty cell rather than a word, because there is none.
Details
Details The heading on the page is given beside the name because two of them
Details carry an ampersand and a space, and a name in this specification is an
Details identifier.
Examples: GroupOfType
| AccountType        | AccountGroup     | Heading          | Listed |
| Checking           | Banking          | Banking          | true   |
| Savings            | Banking          | Banking          | true   |
| Cash               | Banking          | Banking          | true   |
| CreditCard         | Credit           | Credit           | true   |
| LineOfCredit       | Credit           | Credit           | true   |
| Brokerage          | Investments      | Investments      | true   |
| IRA                | Investments      | Investments      | true   |
| HSA                | Investments      | Investments      | true   |
| Retirement401k     | Investments      | Investments      | true   |
| Mortgage           | LoanAndDebt      | Loan~&~Debt      | true   |
| AutoLoan           | LoanAndDebt      | Loan~&~Debt      | true   |
| PersonalLoan       | LoanAndDebt      | Loan~&~Debt      | true   |
| OtherDebt          | LoanAndDebt      | Loan~&~Debt      | true   |
| RealEstate         | PropertyAndAsset | Property~&~Asset | true   |
| Vehicle            | PropertyAndAsset | Property~&~Asset | true   |
| OtherAsset         | PropertyAndAsset | Property~&~Asset | true   |
| AccountsReceivable | Business         | Business         | true   |
| AccountsPayable    | Business         | Business         | true   |
| TransferIn         | Transfer         | Transfer         | true   |
| TransferOut        | Transfer         | Transfer         | true   |
| Income             | Banking          |                  | false  |
| Expense            | Banking          |                  | false  |
| Equity             | Banking          |                  | false  |
# A tilde in a cell is a space, so the heading of the fourth group reads
# "Loan & Debt". The AccountGroup column has to hold something for a category
# and holds Banking, which Listed being false is what makes harmless.

Attributes GroupOfType
| Attribute    | Type         | Default  |
| AccountType  | AccountType  | Checking |
| AccountGroup | AccountGroup | Banking  |
| Heading      | Text         | none     |
| Listed       | Boolean      | true     |

Attributes AccountListRow
Description One line of the account list.
Details A group heading carries the total of the accounts under it and names no
Details account; an account names no group. The groups are listed in the order
Details they are declared, and a group with nothing in it is left out rather
Details than shown empty.
Details
Details Indent is the depth on the page: a group heading is 0, an account under
Details it is 1, and a child of that account is 2.
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Group     | Text        | none    |
| Account   | AccountPath | none    |
| Name      | Text        | none    |
| Indent    | Integer     | 0       |
| Balance   | Money       | 0.00    |
| IsHeading | Boolean     | false   |

