# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reviewing an import in the second pane
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description An import is shown in the split pane rather than in a dialog of its
Description own, so that the register it is about to change is beside it while it
Description is read. Nothing reaches the book until it is accepted.

Attributes ImportReviewRow
Description One row of an import waiting to be reviewed. Account is where the
Description money moved; Category is the other side as the import worked it out.
| Attribute   | Type              | Default    |
| Line        | Integer           | 0          |
| Date        | Date              | 2026-01-01 |
| Payee       | PayeeName         | none       |
| Account     | AccountPath       | none       |
| Category    | AccountPath       | none       |
| Amount      | Money             | 0.00       |
| Disposition | ImportDisposition | New        |
| Accepted    | Boolean           | true       |
| Identifier  | FitId             | none       |
| Source      | ImportSource      | Ofx        |
| RawName     | Text              | none       |
| Memo        | Text              | none       |
| CheckNo     | CheckNumber       | none       |
| Cleared     | ClearedStatus     | Cleared    |

Define AnImportOfThree
Description The import the next several scenarios all read. A scenario cannot
Description take a table from the scenario before it: every generated test stands
Description alone, so the rows are named here and asked for by name.
| Line | Date       | Payee         | Account         | Category               | Amount  | Disposition |
